.\" robodr-commission(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-commission/src/main.rs. Keep the two in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-COMMISSION 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-commission \- learn, review, lock and verify a RoboDR model profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-commission learn
.RB ( \-\-events
.IR run.jsonl " | "
.B \-\-pcap
.IR run.pcap[ng] )
\&...
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-margin
.IR 1.1 ]
.RB [ \-\-min\-samples
.IR 30 ]
.RB [ \-\-ceiling\-linear
.IR M_PER_S ]
.RB [ \-\-ceiling\-joint
.IR RAD_PER_S ]
.RB [ \-\-hard\-cap\-linear
.IR 10 ]
.RB [ \-\-hard\-cap\-joint
.IR 10 ]
.RB [ \-\-min\-announcements
.IR 2 ]
.RB [ \-\-min\-duration
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-accept\-participant
.IR GUID ]...
.RB [ \-\-motion\-topic
.IR /T ]...
.RB [ \-\-discovery\-server
.IR PREFIX | PREFIX@IP | IP ]...
.RB [ \-\-trusted\-discovery\-server
.IR PREFIX | PREFIX@IP | IP ]...
.RB [ \-\-learn\-readers ]
.B \-\-out
.I profile.json
.RB [ \-\-signoff
.IR signoff.json ]
.RB [ \-\-report
.IR report.json ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission lock
.B \-\-in
.I profile.json
.B \-\-signoff
.I signoff.json
.B \-\-out
.I locked.json
.B \-\-operators
.I operators.json
.RB [ \-\-motion\-quorum
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-manifest ]
.RB ( \-\-parent
.IR previous\-locked.json " | "
.B \-\-platform
.I P
.B \-\-profile\-version
.IR N )
.RB [ \-\-unit\-id
.IR U ]
.RB [ \-\-sign\-key
.IR signing.key ]
.RB [ \-\-trusted\-keys
.IR trust.json ]
.RB [ \-\-locked\-at
.IR UNIX_SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-hard\-cap\-linear
.IR 10 ]
.RB [ \-\-hard\-cap\-joint
.IR 10 ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission sign
.B \-\-profile
.I locked.json
.B \-\-sign\-key
.I signing.key
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission verify\-profile
.B \-\-profile
.I locked.json
.B \-\-trusted\-keys
.I trust.json
.RB [ \-\-expect\-platform
.IR P ]
.RB [ \-\-expect\-unit
.IR U ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.IR profile\-state.json ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-rollback
.IR sha256:HEX ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission keygen
.B \-\-out
.I signing.key
.B \-\-trust\-out
.I trust.json
.RB [ \-\-key\-id
.IR ID ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission trust\-keys
.B \-\-out
.I trust.json
.B \-\-pub
.IR KEY.pub " ..."
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission migrate\-legacy
.B \-\-in
.I legacy\-locked.json
.B \-\-out
.I locked.json
.B \-\-platform
.I P
.B \-\-profile\-version
.I N
.B \-\-operator
.I NAME
.B \-\-sign\-key
.I signing.key
.RB [ \-\-unit\-id
.IR U ]
.RB [ \-\-locked\-at
.IR UNIX_SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission signoff
.B \-\-in
.I profile.json
.B \-\-out
.I signoff.json
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission signoff
.B \-\-signoff
.I signoff.json
.B \-\-sign\-key
.I operator.key
.RB [ \-\-in
.IR profile.json ]
.RB [ \-\-operators
.IR operators.json ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission operators
.B \-\-out
.I operators.json
.B \-\-operator
.IR NAME = KEY.pub " ..."
.RB [ \-\-motion\-quorum
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission diff
.I old.json new.json
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission check
.B \-\-profile
.I locked.json
.RB ( \-\-events
.IR f " | "
.B \-\-pcap
.IR f )
\&...
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission merge
.B \-\-out
.I merged.json
.I a.json b.json
\&...
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.PP
.B robodr\-commission
.RB ( help " | " \-\-help " | " \-h " | " version " | " \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-commission
builds the model profile that RoboDR enforces for one robot model.
It is an offline, operator\-run tool, not a service: it reads recorded runs
and writes files, and never touches the robot bus or the running daemons.
.PP
The workflow is
.B learn
(observe a clean run and write a draft profile plus a sign\-off list),
human review of the sign\-off list,
.B lock
(seal, version and sign the reviewed draft),
.B verify\-profile
(the loaders' trust check, read\-only), then
.B check
(replay further runs against the locked profile).
.B diff
compares two profiles,
.B merge
combines drafts, and
.B signoff
creates a conservative sign\-off list for an edited or merged draft.
.SH INPUTS
.TP
.BI \-\-events " file"
JSON Lines of RobotEvent.
.TP
.BI \-\-pcap " file"
pcap or pcapng capture of the robot bus (discovery only: participants,
writers, readers).
.PP
Both repeat and mix; every file is one run.
.SH LEARN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name recorded in the profile.
.TP
.BI \-\-margin " F"
Margin applied to learned motion envelopes (shown default: 1.1).
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-samples " N"
Minimum motion samples per channel (shown default: 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-ceiling\-linear " M_PER_S\fR, " \-\-ceiling\-joint " RAD_PER_S"
Ceilings for learned linear and joint envelopes.
.TP
.BI \-\-hard\-cap\-linear " V\fR, " \-\-hard\-cap\-joint " V"
No envelope exceeds these hard caps (shown default: 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-announcements " N\fR, " \-\-min\-duration " SECS"
Anti\-poisoning: participants announced fewer than
.B \-\-min\-announcements
times (shown default: 2), or, in captures, seen for less than
.B \-\-min\-duration
seconds (0 to 86400), are quarantined: not learned, nor their endpoints or
motion samples.
.TP
.BI \-\-accept\-participant " GUID"
Override the quarantine for a participant (repeatable). It becomes a
sign\-off item.
.TP
.BI \-\-motion\-topic " /T"
Treat this topic as a motion channel (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-discovery\-server " PREFIX|PREFIX@IP|IP"
A known discovery server (repeatable; at most 32): an endpoint it relays
for another participant is attributed to that owner, never to the server,
and is not flagged when the owner is accepted and announced the same
endpoint itself from a commissioned IP. Anything else it relays is not
learned and becomes an
.B endpoint_sender_mismatch
sign\-off item naming the server. Participant announcements it relays are
ignored by the anti\-poisoning gate.
.TP
.BI \-\-trusted\-discovery\-server " PREFIX|PREFIX@IP|IP"
A trusted discovery server: its relayed participant announcements count
for the owner's gate (as the pseudo\-address
.BR relay: \fIserver\fR,
never the server's IP), and endpoints it relays for an accepted owner are
learned. Relays for owners that are not accepted are still flagged. Mirrors
the sensor pipeline's
.B discovery_servers
binding option; trusting a server means trusting whatever it relays.
.TP
.B \-\-learn\-readers
Also learn reader_topics, which turns reader\-topic enforcement on (off by
default: a policy choice for the OEM).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " profile.json"
Draft profile (required). Written with
.BR locked:\ false .
.TP
.BI \-\-signoff " signoff.json"
Sign\-off list (default
.IB out .signoff.json\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-report " report.json"
Machine\-readable learning report.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Do not print the report on stdout.
.SH SIGN-OFF AND LOCK
.B learn
writes a sign\-off list (one item per risky finding: motion writers, late,
brief or multi\-IP participants, outliers, sender mismatches, ...), bound to
the exact draft bytes
.RB ( profile_sha256 )
and to its own item set
.RB ( items_sha256 ).
The operator reviews every item, sets
.B \(dqconfirmed\(dq: true
and fills
.BR \(dqoperator\(dq .
.PP
Those digests are plain hashes: anyone who can write the files can recompute
them. The decision is made authentic by the operator's
.B signature:
.PP
.RS
.B robodr\-commission signoff \-\-signoff
.I S
.B \-\-sign\-key
.I OP.key
.RE
.PP
signs the exact bytes of the confirmed list (Ed25519, robodr\-blackbox key
file
.BR robodr\-blackbox\-key/v2 ,
secret file mode 0600, from
.B keygen
or
.BR "robodr\-blackbox keygen" )
and adds the signature to
.IB S .sig
.RB ( robodr\-signoff\-sigs/v1 ).
It refuses a list that is not fully confirmed, names no operator, has a
broken item digest, or (with
.BR \-\-in )
belongs to another draft or lacks a required item; with
.B \-\-operators
it also refuses a key that is not listed. Further operators sign the same
bytes. Editing the list afterwards voids every signature; re\-signing then
needs
.B \-\-force
(discarding the old signatures).
.PP
.B robodr\-commission operators
builds the
.B operators trust list
.RB ( robodr\-operators/v1 )
from public key files, binding each key to an operator name, with
.B motion_quorum
(default 1). It is refused at load if it is a symlink or writable by
group/others, lists a key id or a public key twice, or asks for a quorum
above its number of distinct operators.
.PP
.B lock \-\-operators
.I operators.json
refuses (exit 1, every reason listed) unless the list belongs to the draft,
names an operator and confirms every item, its item set is intact, the
floor recomputed from the draft is covered (a confirmed motion review per
motion channel, a confirmed
.B envelope_dimension_unbounded
item per motion dimension left unlimited), every signature in
.IB S .sig
verifies under a listed key (one bad or unknown signature refuses: fail
closed), the named operator is among the signers (so
.B locked_by
is an authenticated identity), and, when the list has motion items
.RB ( motion_writer ,
.BR motion_unattributed ,
.BR motion_channel_unreviewed ),
at least
.B motion_quorum
distinct operators (names, not keys) signed: the two\-person rule.
.B \-\-motion\-quorum
raises the quorum for one lock, never lowers it.
.PP
.B Output manifest.
Each output is published atomically, but a power loss between files could
leave a new draft beside an old list or report. So
.B learn
writes
.IB out .manifest.json
.B last
(after removing a stale one): the draft's and report's SHA\-256 and the
list's
.B profile_sha256
and
.BR items_sha256 .
.B lock
refuses a draft whose manifest is missing or does not match the draft, the
list or the report;
.B check
refuses a draft whose manifest does not match (a draft without one, e.g.
from
.BR merge ,
is checked with a note).
.B lock \-\-no\-manifest
skips the check for drafts made before manifests existed. A manifest
detects torn and mixed\-up sets, not forgery.
.PP
.B signoff \-\-in
.I profile.json
.B \-\-out
.I S
builds a conservative list for an edited or merged draft (every participant
and motion channel confirmed individually) and writes the draft's manifest
(replacing a stale one; a manifest that still matches needs
.BR \-\-force ).
.PP
Trust model: trusted are the operators trust list (install it as carefully
as the profile trust file), the operators' secret keys and the
commissioning workstation while
.B learn
runs. Anyone else with write access can delete items and recompute the
digests, but cannot produce a valid operator signature. A careless or
colluding operator (or quorum) can still confirm anything: the signature
makes it a named decision, not a correct one. No key expiry or revocation
list (remove the key from the list). The Ed25519 code is not audited.
.PP
A locked profile is sealed; the sensor refuses a locked profile whose seal
does not match.
.SH VERSIONING AND SIGNING
.B lock
stamps the profile with
.B metadata :
.B schema_version
(1),
.B profile_version
(monotonic, >= 1),
.B platform
and optional
.BR unit_id ,
.B locked_by
(the sign\-off operator),
.B locked_at
(Unix seconds; \fB\-\-locked\-at\fR for reproducible output) and
.BR parent_digest .
With
.BI \-\-parent " previous\-locked.json"
the version defaults to the parent's + 1 (an explicit
.B \-\-profile\-version
must be higher), platform and unit default to the parent's, the model must
match, and the parent file's
.B sha256:
digest is recorded as
.B parent_digest
(rollback lineage). With
.B \-\-trusted\-keys
the parent's own signature is checked first. Without a parent,
.B \-\-platform
and
.B \-\-profile\-version
are required.
.PP
.BI \-\-sign\-key " signing.key"
writes the detached signature
.IB out .sig
together with the profile: Ed25519 over the domain tag
.B robodr\-profile\-sig/v1
and the exact sealed bytes. The signing key is a
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)
key file
.RB ( robodr\-blackbox\-key/v2 ,
.BR \(dqkind\(dq: \(dqsecret\(dq ,
.BR \(dqalgorithm\(dq: \(dqed25519\(dq ;
mode 0600), the one RoboDR key format: made by
.BR keygen ,
which also writes its public key file
.IB signing.key .pub
(mode 0644) and the
.B robodr\-profile\-trust/v1
file holding the public key, or by
.BR "robodr\-blackbox keygen" .
.B trust\-keys
builds a trust file from one or more Ed25519
.B .pub
files (a file with secret material is refused). A public key file cannot
sign. Keep the signing key on the commissioning
station, never on the robot; install only the trust file on the robot.
.B sign
signs an already locked profile (offline signing station).
.PP
The loaders (sensor pipeline,
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-ros2\-watch (1))
enforce a locked profile only if it carries metadata and a valid signature
from a trusted key; otherwise they run observe\-only and report
.BR robot.ros2.profile_refused .
.B verify\-profile
runs the same check and prints the file digest; with
.B \-\-state
it also evaluates anti\-rollback against a state file without writing it
(exit 0 trusted, 1 refused).
.PP
.B Legacy profiles.
A profile locked before metadata existed (sealed, no
.BR metadata )
is refused by every loader.
.B migrate\-legacy
re\-issues it with metadata and a signature, content unchanged, the
legacy file's digest recorded as
.BR parent_digest .
Review the content before migrating: migration vouches for it again.
.SH FILE HANDLING
Outputs never overwrite an existing file or follow a symlink unless
.B \-\-force
(symlinks are refused even then). Every output is written atomically
(temporary file, fsync, rename). The outputs of one command must be distinct
from each other and from its inputs. A failed
.B learn
writes nothing; its output manifest is written last (see
.BR "SIGN-OFF AND LOCK" ).
Profiles are loaded strictly (regular file, size cap, no
unknown keys, sealed if locked, metadata only on locked profiles).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
OK / clean.
.TP
.B 1
Negative result: deviations found, profiles differ, lock refused, profile
not trusted (\fBverify\-profile\fR).
.TP
.B 2
Usage, input or I/O error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
robodr\-commission learn \-\-pcap run1.pcapng \-\-pcap run2.pcapng \e
    \-\-model ugv\-x \-\-out draft.json \-\-report report.json
$EDITOR draft.json.signoff.json      # review, confirm, set operator
robodr\-commission keygen \-\-out alice.key \-\-trust\-out /dev/null \-\-key\-id alice
robodr\-commission operators \-\-out operators.json \e
    \-\-operator Alice=alice.key.pub \-\-operator Bob=bob.key.pub \-\-motion\-quorum 2
robodr\-commission signoff \-\-signoff draft.json.signoff.json \e
    \-\-sign\-key alice.key \-\-in draft.json \-\-operators operators.json
robodr\-commission signoff \-\-signoff draft.json.signoff.json \-\-sign\-key bob.key
robodr\-commission keygen \-\-out oem\-profile.key \e
    \-\-trust\-out profile\-trust.json \-\-key\-id oem\-ugv\-x\-2026
robodr\-commission lock \-\-in draft.json \e
    \-\-signoff draft.json.signoff.json \-\-operators operators.json \e
    \-\-out locked.json \e
    \-\-platform ugv\-x \-\-profile\-version 1 \-\-sign\-key oem\-profile.key
robodr\-commission verify\-profile \-\-profile locked.json \e
    \-\-trusted\-keys profile\-trust.json
robodr\-commission check \-\-profile locked.json \-\-pcap run3.pcapng
# next version of the same lineage
robodr\-commission lock \-\-in draft2.json \-\-signoff draft2.json.signoff.json \e
    \-\-operators operators.json \-\-out locked2.json \-\-parent locked.json \-\-sign\-key oem\-profile.key
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-ros2\-watch (1),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-pulsard (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
